{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OviOneKenoby/ESP32-WROVER-Internet-radio/pulls/5","id":4814576484,"node_id":"PR_kwDOT511uM8AAAABHvibZA","html_url":"https://github.com/OviOneKenoby/ESP32-WROVER-Internet-radio/pull/5","diff_url":"https://github.com/OviOneKenoby/ESP32-WROVER-Internet-radio/pull/5.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/OviOneKenoby/ESP32-WROVER-Internet-radio/pull/5.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OviOneKenoby/ESP32-WROVER-Internet-radio/issues/5","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OviOneKenoby/ESP32-WROVER-Internet-radio/pulls/5/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OviOneKenoby/ESP32-WROVER-Internet-radio/pulls/5/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OviOneKenoby/ESP32-WROVER-Internet-radio/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OviOneKenoby/ESP32-WROVER-Internet-radio/issues/5/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OviOneKenoby/ESP32-WROVER-Internet-radio/statuses/cf37f83b181e859e392d9f3972ee0d9f6ed333aa","number":5,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Preserve Wi-Fi TX progress by moving large lwIP allocations to PSRAM","user":{"login":"OviOneKenoby","id":26651380,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NjUxMzgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26651380?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/OviOneKenoby","html_url":"https://github.com/OviOneKenoby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OviOneKenoby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OviOneKenoby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OviOneKenoby/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OviOneKenoby/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OviOneKenoby/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OviOneKenoby/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OviOneKenoby/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OviOneKenoby/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OviOneKenoby/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Bluetooth playback plus root/browser traffic could exhaust internal DMA-capable memory during Wi-Fi TX conversion. In the reproduced failure, four 1622-byte conversion allocations remained represented by retained pbuf references; the cache reached `headNULL`, TX returned persistent `NO_MEM`, and ping/HTTP stopped while association, the main loop, and Bluetooth audio remained active.\n\nThis PR adds bounded diagnostics that established that sequence and an explicit `esp32-lwip-psram` corrective profile. The profile prefers PSRAM for lwIP `mem_malloc` requests of at least 512 bytes, then falls back once to the original allocator. It preserves Wi-Fi TX dynamic32/cache4, driver retry behavior, HTTP payloads, GPIO behavior, and the pinned framework. It adds no automatic reconnect or reboot. The default PlatformIO environment remains `esp32-dev`; the corrective policy is selected explicitly with `pio run -e esp32-lwip-psram`.\n\nHardware validation used the exact 1.1.11 binary and ELF (`124e84801b06`). Across two independent boots, root, diagnostics, ping, and Bluetooth audio remained available. Each run observed three transient 1622-byte Wi-Fi conversion allocation failures followed by requeue, resumed conversion, continued TX, and balanced ref/free counts. Neither run reproduced cache `headNULL`, TX `NO_MEM`, retained pbuf references, disconnects, or service loss.\n\nThe owner accepted this as a functional PASS. The evidence has two explicit limits: the strict zero-DMA-failure criterion did not pass, and the second sustained run covered about 3 minutes 44.566 seconds rather than the planned 30 minutes. The result supports recovery and availability under the tested traffic; it does not claim that all internal-memory pressure has been eliminated or inventory the driver's private cache pool.\n\nValidation:\n\n- 2,367 deterministic host checks pass.\n- 7 PSRAM policy wrapper cases pass.\n- 20 exact-ELF classifier checks pass, including rejection of the historical bad operand and all 18 mutations.\n- TEST_01: 377 ping replies with no timeout/unreachable; TX refs/frees 438/438 after about 123 seconds of recovery observation.\n- SUSTAINED_01: 224 ping replies with no timeout/unreachable; TX refs/frees 463/463 after the final transient failures.\n- Exact candidate BIN/ELF, SHA-256 manifests, raw serial/ping logs, decoded traces, and Romanian reports are committed under `artifacts/NETWORK_VALIDATION_1.1.11_PSRAM/`.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-10T21:31:23Z","updated_at":"2026-10-11T17:09:13Z","closed_at":"2026-10-11T17:09:13Z","merged_at":"2026-10-11T17:09:12Z","merge_commit_sha":"5fb92c95d228d744d1182ae3956e850c5be2f277","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"OviOneKenoby:tuner/wifi-observability","ref":"tuner/wifi-observability","repo":{"id":1335719352,"node_id":"R_kgDOT511uA","name":"ESP32-WROVER-Internet-radio","full_name":"OviOneKenoby/ESP32-WROVER-Internet-radio","owner":{"login":"OviOneKenoby","id":26651380,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NjUxMzgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26651380?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/OviOneKenoby","html_url":"https://github.com/OviOneKenoby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OviOneKenoby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OviOneKenoby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OviOneKenoby/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OviOneKenoby/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OviOneKenoby/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OviOneKenoby/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OviOneKenoby/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.c